    "{\n",
    " \"cells\": [\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Data Analytics Assignment — Question 1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Understanding Data & Attribute Classification\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Dataset:** insurance.csv (1,338 records)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Part A – Attribute Type Identification (3 Marks)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"| Attribute | Type | Justification |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|-----------|------|---------------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **age** | Discrete | Integer count of years; countable whole numbers with no fractional meaning. |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **sex** | Nominal | Two categories (male/female) with no inherent ordering. |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **bmi** | Continuous | Measurable real-valued number on a continuous scale (e.g., 27.9, 33.77). |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **children** | Discrete | Countable integer representing number of children (0, 1, 2, ...). |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **smoker** | Nominal | Binary categorical label (yes/no) with no ordinal relationship. |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **region** | Nominal | Geographic categories (southwest, southeast, northwest, northeast) with no natural order. |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| **charges** | Continuous | Measurable monetary amount that can take any real value within a range. |\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Part B – Data Extraction & Cleaning (4 Marks)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Import required libraries\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import pandas as pd\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import numpy as np\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\\n\",\n",
    "    \"import seaborn as sns\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Set display options\\n\",\n",
    "    \"pd.set_option('display.max_columns', None)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"pd.set_option('display.width', None)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Task 1: Load the dataset from Google Drive\\n\",\n",
    "    \"url = \\\"https://drive.google.com/uc?export=download&id=1oyN6CXzbJq42dL5Jqkn1cP83Hu93CD6q\\\"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df = pd.read_csv(url)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Display first 10 rows\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"=== First 10 Rows ===\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(df.head(10))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Display dataset info\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"\\\\n=== Dataset Info ===\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df.info()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Task 2: Check for missing values and duplicates\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"=== Missing Values ===\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(df.isnull().sum())\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"\\\\nTotal missing values: {df.isnull().sum().sum()}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"\\\\n=== Duplicate Records ===\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"duplicates = df.duplicated().sum()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Number of duplicate rows: {duplicates}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Handle duplicates if present\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if duplicates > 0:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    df = df.drop_duplicates()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"Duplicates removed. New shape: {df.shape}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"No duplicates found — no action needed.\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Task 3: Identify data inconsistencies\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"=== Descriptive Statistics ===\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(df.describe())\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Check for negative charges\\n\",\n",
    "    \"negative_charges = (df['charges'] < 0).sum()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"\\\\nNegative charges found: {negative_charges}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Check for unrealistic BMI values (< 10 or > 60)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"unrealistic_bmi = ((df['bmi'] < 10) | (df['bmi'] > 60)).sum()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Unrealistic BMI values (<10 or >60): {unrealistic_bmi}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Check for negative age\\n\",\n",
    "    \"negative_age = (df['age'] < 0).sum()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Negative age values: {negative_age}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Check for negative children count\\n\",\n",
    "    \"negative_children = (df['children'] < 0).sum()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Negative children count: {negative_children}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"\\\\n=== Conclusion ===\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if negative_charges == 0 and unrealistic_bmi == 0 and negative_age == 0 and negative_children == 0:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"No obvious data inconsistencies detected. The dataset appears clean.\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"Some inconsistencies detected — review required.\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Task 4: Convert categorical attributes to numeric\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# --- Encoding 'smoker' as binary (0/1) ---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Explanation: 'smoker' has two categories (yes/no). We map 'yes' -> 1 and 'no' -> 0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# to create a binary numeric variable suitable for correlation analysis and modeling.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df['smoker_encoded'] = df['smoker'].map({'yes': 1, 'no': 0})\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# --- Encoding 'region' using one-hot encoding (get_dummies) ---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Explanation: 'region' is a nominal variable with 4 categories and no inherent order.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Using get_dummies creates 4 separate binary columns (one per region), avoiding\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# artificial ordinal relationships that label encoding would introduce.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"df_encoded = pd.get_dummies(df, columns=['region'], prefix='region', dtype=int)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"=== Smoker Encoding ===\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(df[['smoker', 'smoker_encoded']].head(10))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"\\\\n=== Region One-Hot Encoding (first 10 rows) ===\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"region_cols = [col for col in df_encoded.columns if col.startswith('region_')]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(df_encoded[['region_northeast', 'region_northwest', 'region_southeast', 'region_southwest']].head(10))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"\\\\nOriginal shape: {df.shape}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Encoded shape: {df_encoded.shape}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"\\\\nNew columns added: {region_cols}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Part C – Data Viewing (4 Marks)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Task 5: Geometric View — Scatter plot of BMI vs. Charges, color-coded by smoker status\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Separate data by smoker status\\n\",\n",
    "    \"smokers = df[df['smoker'] == 'yes']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"non_smokers = df[df['smoker'] == 'no']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.scatter(non_smokers['bmi'], non_smokers['charges'], \\n\",\n",
    "    \"            c='blue', label='Non-Smoker', alpha=0.5, s=30)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.scatter(smokers['bmi'], smokers['charges'], \\n\",\n",
    "    \"            c='red', label='Smoker', alpha=0.5, s=30)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.xlabel('BMI', fontsize=12)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.ylabel('Insurance Charges ($)', fontsize=12)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title('BMI vs. Insurance Charges (Color-coded by Smoker Status)', fontsize=14)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.legend()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"\\\\n=== Observation ===\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"Smokers (red) consistently have higher insurance charges across all BMI values,\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"forming a distinct upper cluster. Non-smokers (blue) show lower charges with a\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"moderate positive trend — as BMI increases, charges tend to rise slightly.\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"This suggests smoker status is a stronger predictor of charges than BMI alone.\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Task 6: Algebraic View — Data matrix for first 10 rows (numeric attributes only)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"data_matrix = df[['age', 'bmi', 'children', 'charges']].head(10).copy()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"data_matrix.index = range(1, 11)  # 1-based indexing\\n\",\n",
    "    \"data_matrix.columns = ['age', 'bmi', 'children', 'charges']\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"=== Data Matrix (First 10 Rows — Numeric Attributes) ===\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"\\\\nRows = observations (patients), Columns = attributes (features)\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(data_matrix.round(2))\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Task 7: Probabilistic View — Histogram with KDE curve for charges\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Plot histogram with KDE\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sns.histplot(df['charges'], bins=50, kde=True, color='steelblue', \\n\",\n",
    "    \"             edgecolor='black', alpha=0.7)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.xlabel('Insurance Charges ($)', fontsize=12)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.ylabel('Frequency', fontsize=12)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title('Probability Distribution of Insurance Charges', fontsize=14)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.grid(True, alpha=0.3)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Calculate skewness\\n\",\n",
    "    \"skewness = df['charges'].skew()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"\\\\n=== Distribution Analysis ===\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"Skewness coefficient: {skewness:.2f}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"if skewness > 1:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"The distribution is RIGHT-SKEWED (positively skewed).\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"Most patients have lower charges, with a long tail of high-charge outliers.\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"elif skewness < -1:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"The distribution is LEFT-SKEWED (negatively skewed).\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"else:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(\\\"The distribution is approximately symmetric.\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Part D – Correlation Analysis (4 Marks)\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Task 8 & 9: Compute and visualize correlation matrix\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Select numeric columns for correlation\\n\",\n",
    "    \"numeric_df = df[['age', 'bmi', 'children', 'charges', 'smoker_encoded']]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Compute Pearson correlation matrix\\n\",\n",
    "    \"corr_matrix = numeric_df.corr(method='pearson')\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"=== Pearson Correlation Matrix ===\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"display(corr_matrix.round(3))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Plot heatmap\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.figure(figsize=(8, 6))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"sns.heatmap(corr_matrix, annot=True, fmt='.3f', cmap='coolwarm', \\n\",\n",
    "    \"            center=0, square=True, linewidths=1, \\n\",\n",
    "    \"            xticklabels=['age', 'bmi', 'children', 'charges', 'smoker'],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            yticklabels=['age', 'bmi', 'children', 'charges', 'smoker'],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            cbar_kws={'label': 'Pearson Correlation Coefficient'})\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.title('Correlation Heatmap — Numeric Attributes', fontsize=14)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null,\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Task 10: Identify highest positive and negative correlations\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Extract upper triangle (excluding diagonal)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"upper_triangle = corr_matrix.where(\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    np.triu(np.ones(corr_matrix.shape, dtype=bool), k=1)\\n\",\n",
    "    \")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Find max and min correlations\\n\",\n",
    "    \"max_corr_pair = upper_triangle.stack().idxmax()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"max_corr_value = upper_triangle.stack().max()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"min_corr_pair = upper_triangle.stack().idxmin()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"min_corr_value = upper_triangle.stack().min()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"=== Correlation Analysis Results ===\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"\\\\nHighest POSITIVE correlation: {max_corr_pair[0]} ↔ {max_corr_pair[1]}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"  Correlation coefficient: r = {max_corr_value:.3f}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"\\\\nHighest NEGATIVE correlation: {min_corr_pair[0]} ↔ {min_corr_pair[1]}\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(f\\\"  Correlation coefficient: r = {min_corr_value:.3f}\\\")\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### Task 11 — Correlation Discussion\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"**Discussion:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The correlation analysis reveals that **smoker status has the strongest positive correlation with insurance charges** (r = 0.787), indicating that smokers incur significantly higher medical costs than non-smokers. This is by far the most dominant demographic predictor in the dataset. Age shows a moderate positive correlation with charges (r ≈ 0.30), reflecting the natural increase in healthcare needs as patients grow older. BMI exhibits a weaker but still positive correlation (r ≈ 0.20), suggesting that higher body mass index is associated with elevated charges, though the relationship is less pronounced. The number of children shows a slight negative correlation with charges, which may indicate that families with more children are relatively younger and healthier overall.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"The highest negative correlation is between **age and smoker status** (r = −0.026), which is very weak and suggests these two variables are essentially independent — smokers are distributed fairly evenly across age groups. The weak inter-correlations among demographic predictors (age, BMI, children) mean they provide largely independent information, making them valuable as combined features in a multivariate model. The dominant smoker–charges relationship (r = 0.787) underscores the actuarial principle that tobacco use is the primary risk factor driving healthcare expenditure, consistent with well-documented links between tobacco and chronic diseases such as cardiovascular disease, respiratory illness, and cancer.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Summary of Deliverables\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| Part | Deliverable | Status |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"|------|-------------|--------|\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| A | Attribute classification table with justifications | ✅ |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| B | Data loading, cleaning, duplicate handling, encoding | ✅ |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| C | Scatter plot, data matrix, histogram with KDE | ✅ |\\n\",\n",
    "    \"| D | Correlation heatmap + written analysis | ✅ |\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  }\n",
    " ],\n",
